meta {
  name: Create Node
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{serveUrl}}/config/nodes/{{nodeName}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "url": "http://192.168.1.55:9000",
    "driver": "linux"
  }
}

docs {
  Adds or replaces the node {{nodeName}} (common.NodeConfig) in the config
  served by `realm serve`. The name is taken from the path; a `name` in the
  body is optional but must match it.

  A whole new config is instanced with the node before replacing the current
  one, so any config error (missing or unknown driver, invalid url...) is
  rejected and the current config is kept. Loads already running on a
  replaced node stay on it.

  After the change, the cluster state is planned on the state file and, if
  the cluster is running, rolled out to it. The response `cluster` field
  holds the planned diff (`plan`), whether the cluster runs it (`updated`)
  and why planning or updating failed (`error`); the config change is kept
  even if they fail.

  Responses: 201 created, 200 replaced, 400 invalid node or config.
  Body: {"node": {...}, "cluster": {...}}
}
